{"title":"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2011 USAJMO Problems\">2011 USAJMO #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems\">2011 USAMO #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<p><i>This problem is from both the 2011 USAJMO and the 2011 USAMO, so both problems redirect here.</i>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the assertion that for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, the remainder upon dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c3455b8d6564924f33e1e4ce8b64d2dd90408c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b063495d0243e7bc52c3a7f231362bdc4a03775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is a power of 4. Either prove the assertion or find (with proof) a counter-example.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748375ba3345781f252164e4d576fc9225f8cacf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 25$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is a counter-example.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50e17b16c85abffa5eb2d573d249bb8893bbfad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2^n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />, we see that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/0176a8ae78b39f17fa8c2e3fcd0ce818b851fe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^{2^n} \\equiv 2^{(2^n - kn)} \\pmod{2^n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"19\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de773fd62c8f67652483479bc3d228518e6067a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le m &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> be the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e007759cfa79045da709d374b0753eb6dc6fb99c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\pmod n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />. Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/0431e1fbb8d5eeb5841b565cb4a6d47aa7aa36c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle m &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc6a792020a9c7954d0bfa3777049932ab54fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20a3c572b1ff87e44cdf66b32385c6f6335bbcb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^m &lt; 2^n -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"94\" height=\"12\" />, and thus the remainder in question is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee9a9421a739feb317119bb58c2b92614fdf3488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />. We want to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9647afdc15558e2dc4c384e8c2335878592fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^m \\pmod {2^n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> is an odd power of 2 for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac7b6c4cf0f184855d022997aa40bd6816d04fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, and thus not a power of 4.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bad763c0413edcd3383e906bad4f3b60a4dc40ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle n=p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> for some odd prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/4/b246e4c48b4f56b47ccfbce9ef445390ce04b37f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e27614d4e9a1a6b8139146afc66215328932a3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle \\varphi(p^2) = p^2 - p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />. Since 2 is co-prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afb3174d610cdf92b841942da9e4f73246fda05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fe870528c7b3d0ecdc5f84c2813112e0a88452.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{2^{\\varphi(p^2)} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{p^2}}\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"22\" />\nand thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b55b6774021e1796eb350cfeeddb6b2a2433aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textstyle 2^{p^2} \\equiv 2^{(p^2 - p) + p} \\equiv 2^p \\pmod{p^2}.\\]\" width=\"249\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, for a counter-example, it suffices that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67cf4c4ba8c4d56561b04d8e6cad83aee6005b99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^p \\pmod{p^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> be odd. Choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfbe99f88c157ba2d07d6a353133f8c85347844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle p=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/882f0698e5782d64243dc67f732148fff0d815b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^5 = 32 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c446209a940f37192d5574d7889e9a3749ab0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^{25} \\equiv 7 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" /> and thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfcac31c68c073a53f51850c390f6153b0022e92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textstyle 2^{2^{25}} \\equiv 2^7 \\pmod {2^{25} - 1}.\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96696324902634c9084df1202a9a4e1e9d4d0569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle 2^7$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is not a power of 4, we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lemma (useful for all situations): If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42b7d3157d354071a895f38f54affd8df422b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f080fbc8148083f2b68e88db1ab77ee5b2f5a70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^y - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\nProof: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee597bf5c8f878121e5248bab037ea503e212b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^y \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2^x - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />. Replacing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065d0462782004d830c2bfbda340ff333d710f37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> and dividing out the powers of two should create an easy induction proof which will be left to the reader as an Exercise.\n</p><p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748375ba3345781f252164e4d576fc9225f8cacf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 25$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. We will prove that this case is a counterexample via contradiction.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec451be937b467cb66db472e8bf738e96552f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 = 2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, we will assume there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee07186bb1da947b34f392f5f107294652ed49a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} - 2^{2k}$\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654a7c7010145200d9d8723eda7ce20e98b5723c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/1/ff16a6ec804c98017e8aaaf4fb60279bdbc79c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2k} &lt; 2^n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />. Dividing the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from LHS gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/310a54fa8f6489b45a6023db00a6b56ce05c9e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n - 2k} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654a7c7010145200d9d8723eda7ce20e98b5723c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c741225832b84566b4e90d4816d38d9b36b76e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n - 2k$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748375ba3345781f252164e4d576fc9225f8cacf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 25$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d17714663d32f1d62e9d18c097e76103e5242a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{24} - k$\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Euler's theorem gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d0d686879e478d47537a51125a6726d91b1ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{24} \\equiv 2^4 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dffd25b5c8bdf49473136b8cac32f4c6d9e06cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c095c23c048689b79be3c8d0d16c9fe2d02f192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2k} \\geq 2^{32} &gt; 2^{25} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />, a contradiction. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748375ba3345781f252164e4d576fc9225f8cacf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 25$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is a valid counterexample.\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO\" title=\"2011 USAMO\">2011 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017225300\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 324/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1476/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 129/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9644/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   26.789      1 -total\n 24.11%    6.460      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 22.50%    6.028      1 Template:Duplicate\n 18.59%    4.979      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9291:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017225300 and revision id 152654. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}